  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Tanzania - Capacity Building to Promote Gender-Responsive Legal Literacy and Legal Aid</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Institutional strengthening and capacity building support to promote partnership between government and civil society in gender-responsive legal reformcomma legal literacy and educationcomma and improving the access of the poor to legal services.  The purpose of the Grant is to assist the Recipient to promote gender-responsive legal reform in providing the institutional capacity building support neededcomma through: (i) enhancing dialogue and partnership between the Recipient and civil society; (ii) joint training for key staff from the government and civil society; (iii) strengthening and expansion of legal literacy education and legal aid initiatives; and (iv) joint evaluation of the activities by the Recipient and civil society.</narrative>
  </description>
